---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About ScamLens — decision support against scams"
  description="Why we built ScamLens: explain warning signs with evidence instead of pretending certainty. India-first scam intelligence."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="display-section mt-4">A calm second opinion, not an antivirus scare</h1>
    <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-body-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
      <p>
        ScamLens exists because the moment of doubt — <em>"is this message real?"</em> —
        deserves better than a scary red warning or a meaningless score out of 100.
      </p>
      <p>
        We show our work: every flag comes with the exact quote that triggered it, why it
        matters, and what to do next. Language patterns alone never prove a scam, so we
        never pretend they do. You stay the judge; we're just the lens.
      </p>
      <p>
        We're India-first because that's where global tools fall short — UPI QR tricks,
        Rs 99 courier fees, FASTag phishing and digital arrest don't appear in Western
        pattern libraries. Our scam library documents these patterns openly, for everyone.
      </p>
      <p class="text-body">
        If you've been defrauded: call <a href="tel:1930" class="text-primary-hover hover:underline">1930</a> immediately
        and file at <a href="https://cybercrime.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary-hover hover:underline">cybercrime.gov.in</a>.
        The first hour matters.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a href="/#checker" class="btn btn-primary mt-10 px-6">Try the checker</a>
  </section>
</Layout>
